"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs=self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs||[]).push([[1678],{64065(e,r,a){a.r(r),a.d(r,{comp:()=>n,data:()=>s});var t=a(20641);const o={},n=(0,a(66262).A)(o,[["render",function(e,r){return(0,t.uX)(),(0,t.CE)("div",null,r[0]||(r[0]=[(0,t.Fv)('<h1 id="separate-wp-admin-dashboard" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#separate-wp-admin-dashboard"><span>Separate WP-Admin Dashboard</span></a></h1><p>The <strong>Separate WP-Admin Dashboard</strong> provides marketplace sellers with a dedicated, isolated WordPress backend environment. When enabled, vendors manage their products, orders, transactions, store profile, and customer communication directly within a secure, custom-tailored WordPress administration interface.</p><p>This separate interface keeps vendor operations completely independent from platform administration, ensuring that sellers only access features relevant to their store.</p><hr><h2 id="enabling-separate-vendor-dashboard" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#enabling-separate-vendor-dashboard"><span>Enabling Separate Vendor Dashboard</span></a></h2><p>Marketplace administrators can easily enable or disable the separate backend dashboard from the WordPress administration panel:</p><ol><li>Navigate to <strong>Marketplace &gt; Settings &gt; General</strong>.</li><li>Locate the <strong>Separate Vendor Dashboard</strong> setting checkbox.</li><li>Check the box to activate the separate dashboard for all registered marketplace vendors.</li><li>Click <strong>Save Changes</strong> at the bottom of the page.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="access-control-security-isolation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#access-control-security-isolation"><span>Access Control &amp; Security Isolation</span></a></h2><p>The Separate WP-Admin Dashboard is designed specifically for marketplace vendors. To protect marketplace security and keep the workspace simple and focused, menu options are automatically filtered:</p><h3 id="hidden-administrative-areas" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#hidden-administrative-areas"><span>Hidden Administrative Areas</span></a></h3><p>To prevent accidental changes to core site configuration, general site settings are hidden from vendors:</p><ul><li><strong>Tools</strong></li><li><strong>Global Media Library</strong></li><li><strong>Standard WordPress Posts &amp; Pages</strong></li><li><strong>WooCommerce Core Settings &amp; Store Reports</strong></li><li><strong>Plugins, Themes, and Site User Management</strong></li></ul><h3 id="available-vendor-menus" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#available-vendor-menus"><span>Available Vendor Menus</span></a></h3><p>Vendors have access only to the store-specific tools required for day-to-day operations:</p><ul><li><strong>Dashboard</strong>: Welcome screen and high-level store overview.</li><li><strong>Products</strong>: Catalog management restricted to the vendor&#39;s own items: <ul><li><strong>All Products</strong>: View, search, and edit published products.</li><li><strong>Add new product</strong>: Create new physical, variable, virtual, or downloadable products.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Marketplace</strong>: The core vendor management suite, containing the following dedicated sections: <ul><li><strong>Reports</strong>: Main analytics dashboard displaying total sales, orders, customer metrics, performance graphs, and recent store activity.</li><li><strong>Order History</strong>: Complete order ledger to inspect customer details, monitor fulfillment status, and enter tracking numbers.</li><li><strong>Transactions</strong>: Financial statement tracking gross earnings, platform commission deductions, and payout disbursements.</li><li><strong>Notifications</strong>: Real-time activity log for new orders, customer reviews, and marketplace announcements.</li><li><strong>Shop Followers</strong>: Directory of customers following your shop, with options for direct audience outreach.</li><li><strong>My Profile</strong>: Storefront profile manager to customize store logo, banner, biography, contact info, social links, and payout methods.</li><li><strong>Ask to admin</strong>: Direct inquiry channel to send support questions to marketplace administrators and view conversation history.</li><li><strong>Select And Sell</strong>: Quick catalog tool to claim and sell pre-existing marketplace products without creating listings from scratch.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Comments</strong>: Product reviews and ratings submitted by buyers.</li><li><strong>Profile</strong>: Personal user account settings, email address, and password management.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="managing-products-for-vendors" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#managing-products-for-vendors"><span>Managing Products for Vendors</span></a></h2><p>Vendors can manage their approved products directly from the WordPress administration panel using WooCommerce&#39;s native product editor. The catalog is strictly isolated, ensuring sellers only see and edit their own merchandise under <strong>Products &gt; All Products</strong> and <strong>Products &gt; Add new product</strong>.</p><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Official WooCommerce Product Guides for New Vendors</p><p>To help new vendors quickly learn how to create and manage their store items, refer to the official WooCommerce documentation:</p><ul><li><p><strong><a href="https://woocommerce.com/document/managing-products/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Overview: Managing Products in WooCommerce</a></strong><br> Learn the foundations of product management, including catalog visibility, inventory status, product categories, and attributes.</p></li><li><p><strong><a href="https://woocommerce.com/document/managing-products/add-product/#adding-a-simple-product" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Step-by-Step: Adding a Simple Product</a></strong><br> A detailed walkthrough covering product titles, descriptions, regular and sale pricing, inventory tracking (SKU and stock status), shipping dimensions, and product gallery images.</p></li></ul></div>',20)]))}]]),s=JSON.parse('{"path":"/documentation/vendor-separate-dashboard.html","title":"Separate WP-Admin Dashboard","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Separate WP-Admin Dashboard","description":"Complete user guide for the Separate WP-Admin Dashboard in WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace. Learn how vendors access an isolated WordPress backend to manage products, track orders, view transactions, customize store profiles, and communicate with admins.","head":[["meta",{"name":"keywords","content":"woocommerce separate vendor dashboard, marketplace seller admin panel, vendor backend access wordpress, seller dashboard woocommerce, multi-vendor separate admin, vendor order management wordpress"}],["meta",{"property":"og:title","content":"Separate WP-Admin Dashboard | WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace"}],["meta",{"property":"og:description","content":"Complete user guide for the Separate WP-Admin Dashboard in WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace."}],["meta",{"property":"og:type","content":"article"}]]},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"Enabling Separate Vendor Dashboard","slug":"enabling-separate-vendor-dashboard","link":"#enabling-separate-vendor-dashboard","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Access Control & Security Isolation","slug":"access-control-security-isolation","link":"#access-control-security-isolation","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Hidden Administrative Areas","slug":"hidden-administrative-areas","link":"#hidden-administrative-areas","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Available Vendor Menus","slug":"available-vendor-menus","link":"#available-vendor-menus","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Managing Products for Vendors","slug":"managing-products-for-vendors","link":"#managing-products-for-vendors","children":[]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"documentation/vendor-separate-dashboard.md"}')}}]);